{"parentUuid":"a853df90-8725-499c-bee6-42c8edc66d44","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011J6SsdGQgsrHohcUJdN4ZS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short version: `gotestsum` is a wrapper around `go test`. It runs the same tests, but it parses the JSON test output (`go test -json`) and re-renders it in nicer formats. The actual test execution, build flags, tags, race detector, coverage — all of that is `go test` underneath.\n\nWhat `go test` gives you out of the box:\n- Streams every line of test output as it happens.\n- One line per package at the end (`ok`, `FAIL`, `?`).\n- No grouping; if 200 packages run in parallel, their output interleaves into a wall of text.\n- A FAIL near the top scrolls off-screen by the time you finish.\n- `-v` makes it more verbose, not more readable.\n\nWhat `gotestsum` adds:\n- **Output formats** (`--format`): the most useful are\n  - `pkgname` — one line per package, prints failing package output below. Quiet on success.\n  - `testname` — one line per test (PASS/FAIL/SKIP). Good for slow integration runs.\n  - `dots` — Mocha-style dots. Compact.\n  - `standard-quiet` / `standard-verbose` — closest to `go test` / `go test -v`.\n- **A summary at the end**: counts of passed/failed/skipped, and crucially, a re-printed list of failures so you don't have to scroll. `--hide-summary skipped` (which we use) drops the noise from skipped tests.\n- **`--format-icons text`** — uses ASCII (PASS/FAIL/SKIP) instead of unicode glyphs, which renders correctly on plain terminals and CI logs.\n- **`--format-hide-empty-pkg`** — skips packages with no tests, so you don't see `?` lines for every internal helper package.\n- **JUnit XML output** (`--junitfile`), useful for CI systems that want to parse results.\n- **Rerun-flaky** support (`--rerun-fails`), which `go test` doesn't have.\n- It still passes everything after `--` straight through to `go test`, so you keep `-tags`, `-race`, `-run`, `-count`, etc.\n\nIn our `mise.toml`:\n\n```\ngotestsum --format pkgname --format-icons text --format-hide-empty-pkg --hide-summary skipped -- ./...\n```\n\nis `go test ./...` with: one line per package, ASCII icons, no `?` rows for empty packages, and skipped tests left out of the final summary. On failure, the offending package's output is printed below its line, with a list of failures repeated at the very bottom — so you don't lose the failure when 50 other packages finish after it.\n\nCaveat worth knowing: `test:ci` in our `mise.toml` deliberately stays on raw `go test -tags=integration -race ./...`. CI parses the structured `go test` output, and you don't want a wrapper layered in front of that — keeping it raw also makes failures easier to copy-paste from CI logs into bug reports."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":188913,"output_tokens":1027,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1027,"cache_read_input_tokens":188913,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqPhHJuMP5XYjDYuMtTi","type":"assistant","uuid":"c178590e-a97f-4e55-8121-fa6697255de9","timestamp":"2026-05-08T16:09:42.148Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments_2","sessionId":"13c25299-c79d-4098-bf0a-f1a4eec654c8","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"codex/local-testing-improvements"}
